{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":105960,"duration_api_ms":169449,"num_turns":5,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"47787975-a883-4e25-ad74-3861f22e639d","total_cost_usd":0.4942706000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":1876,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28070,"cache_read_input_tokens":81720,"output_tokens":2094,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28070,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2424,"outputTokens":9809,"cacheReadInputTokens":925516,"cacheCreationInputTokens":57778,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.21624310000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":1876,"outputTokens":2094,"cacheReadInputTokens":81720,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28070,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2780275,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Verified all four amendments against the codebase. The two accumulator-reset bugs (spawn_progress_accum and hatch_success_carry) are confirmed real state-leakage defects — both accumulators persist across population resets and cohort removals with no cleanup path. The CO2 KLA capping asymmetry is confirmed: CO2 caps inside the function while O2 caps at the usage site, a genuine maintainability inconsistency. The DIC rates amendment is rejected — the planner correctly identified that the factual premise is wrong: shipped presets load default.toml which sets nonzero DIC rates (0.08 and 0.12), not 0.0 as claimed.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-98d4fd2c","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified the asymmetry in the codebase. chemistry.rs:57 caps k_la_o2 at 1.0 before multiplying by KLA_CO2_TO_O2_RATIO (0.91), embedding the Euler stability cap inside compute_co2_kla. Meanwhile, dissolved_oxygen.rs:94 caps k_la at 1.0 at the usage site in dissolved_oxygen_terms(). The function's docstring acknowledges this design choice (capping before scaling preserves the physical ratio), but the architectural inconsistency between the two gas paths is real. A future contributor adding a diagnostic display or an alternate CO2 consumer would silently receive capped values without realizing the O2 path handles capping differently. Either renaming to signal the embedded cap or unifying both paths to cap at the same architectural level is a low-cost improvement that prevents a maintainability trap."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-c9a6768a","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment's factual premise is incorrect. All three shipped scenario presets (nano_cycle, medium_planted, warm_room) reference process_params_id = 'default', and the shipped default.toml at crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml sets respiration_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour = 0.08 and photosynthesis_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour = 0.12. The process_preset_to_params() function in tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:356-358 correctly copies these values into runtime ProcessParams. While ProcessParams::default() in Rust does use 0.0, that is only a deserialization fallback — the actual preset-loaded path provides nonzero biological DIC rates. Therefore biological DIC effects ARE enabled in production scenarios, and the claimed gap between test and production behavior does not exist."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-24b63d9b","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed in the code. spawning() returns early at line 424 (no adults) and line 434 (no eligible females) without clearing spawn_progress_accum. The accumulator (biology.rs:164-166) persists its value via deterministic_transfer_count. Critically, reset_hourly_accumulators() at shrimp.rs:909-915 does NOT include spawn_progress_accum, so even a complete population wipeout leaves stale carry. This means a new colony inherits fractional spawn progress from a prior, unrelated colony. The fix — zeroing spawn_progress_accum when spawning continuity is broken (adult count drops to zero) — is straightforward and correct."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-a50e6e2d","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed the same class of state-leakage bug. egg_development() returns early at line 474 (no cohorts and no berried females) without zeroing hatch_success_carry. clamp_berried_to_adults() at biology.rs:590-597 calls trim_egg_cohorts() which removes EggCohort entries but leaves hatch_success_carry untouched. reset_hourly_accumulators() also omits hatch_success_carry. This allows a brand-new clutch to inherit fractional hatch credit from a completely unrelated prior cohort. The fix — clearing hatch_success_carry when all egg cohorts are removed or when the hatch process loses continuity — should be implemented alongside the spawn_progress_accum fix from fr-5-24b63d9b."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"61fcea19-4c53-4393-9c31-244284b3ea56"}
